00:05:31.940 --> 00:05:36.110
Basically, oh, someone
asked what the DNA is from.

00:05:36.110 --> 00:05:39.810
So I actually pulled it out of E. coli,

00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:42.890
so out of these cells.

00:05:42.890 --> 00:05:45.850
I grew them up in a liquid,

00:05:45.850 --> 00:05:50.850
and I put a bunch of chemicals in

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:54.060
to break them open and pull out their DNA

00:05:54.060 --> 00:05:56.670
so I can figure out what it is,

00:05:56.670 --> 00:06:00.530
and then I can put it into other bacteria.

00:06:00.530 --> 00:06:02.970
Basically, I want to use something

00:06:02.970 --> 00:06:06.640
that the E. coli have in their DNA,

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:10.700
and I want to express it or make it happen

00:06:10.700 --> 00:06:14.597
in a different bacteria,
one of the mycobacteria.

00:06:16.150 --> 00:06:20.630
So someone's asked what I mean
by a flame and I'll show you.

00:06:20.630 --> 00:06:24.280
So when you work with bacteria,

00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:27.610
not only do you need to
protect yourself from them,

00:06:27.610 --> 00:06:31.420
we wear the gloves, and if
you work with a pathogen

00:06:31.420 --> 00:06:34.660
or a bacteria that causes a disease,

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:38.040
you have to put on like
a different kind of mask

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:40.063
and special like a lab coat,

00:06:41.450 --> 00:06:44.540
but we also want to make
sure that the bacteria

00:06:44.540 --> 00:06:46.930
that we're working with are protected

00:06:46.930 --> 00:06:48.680
from other bacteria that might

00:06:48.680 --> 00:06:51.740
be on our hands or in our breath.

00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:56.480
So I take ethanol, just
like hand sanitizer

00:06:56.480 --> 00:06:58.730
but without the nice smells,

00:06:58.730 --> 00:07:02.230
and I wipe down my gloves and my area

00:07:02.230 --> 00:07:04.160
to kill all of the bacteria

00:07:04.160 --> 00:07:06.763
that are just hanging out on the surface,

00:07:08.170 --> 00:07:12.300
and then I turn on a legit flame.

00:07:12.300 --> 00:07:15.793
So I'm trying to get it
within both cameras' views.

00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:17.823
Nice.

00:07:19.140 --> 00:07:24.140
And I have a little striker
here, make a little spark,

00:07:24.640 --> 00:07:26.600
some gas comes out of the canister,

00:07:26.600 --> 00:07:29.820
and you can see that there's a flame.

00:07:29.820 --> 00:07:32.543
So this is called sterile technique.

00:07:33.420 --> 00:07:38.100
We use it so that we
can protect the bacteria

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:41.340
from bacteria that we don't want.

00:07:41.340 --> 00:07:46.020
