00:45:34.220 --> 00:45:39.150
But when I was in high school and college,

00:45:39.150 --> 00:45:41.320
we did have lab exams.

00:45:41.320 --> 00:45:44.340
So basically they'd give us a task,

00:45:44.340 --> 00:45:47.390
like make an experiment to test

00:45:47.390 --> 00:45:51.600
if caffeine increases your heart rate,

00:45:51.600 --> 00:45:52.770
and we'd have to figure out

00:45:52.770 --> 00:45:56.760
how to make that
experiment like perfectly.

00:45:56.760 --> 00:46:00.210
So you need to have these
things called controls.

00:46:00.210 --> 00:46:01.830
Basically, you want to make sure

00:46:01.830 --> 00:46:05.250
that this is because of the caffeine.

00:46:05.250 --> 00:46:09.540
So maybe just drinking drinking
increases your heart rate.

00:46:09.540 --> 00:46:13.760
So we'd also have like, oh,
some people drank water,

00:46:13.760 --> 00:46:14.800
and you want to make sure

00:46:14.800 --> 00:46:18.160
you're measuring heart rate the right way.

00:46:18.160 --> 00:46:21.440
So we would do that experiment

00:46:21.440 --> 00:46:25.410
and then write it up
in a formal lab report,

00:46:25.410 --> 00:46:26.640
and then they'd grade that,

00:46:26.640 --> 00:46:30.410
both on how well we
designed the experiment,

00:46:30.410 --> 00:46:32.513
did it, and wrote about it.

